Z||000013||California Kid||10-05-2001||03:54 PM||||I think the big question should be,"Did the car come from the factory that way???" If it did, then you have a very true collectable, and you might be throwing allot of money out the window if you part out the car. As far as I know this option was never offered, but was developed, if you got one, it's a mistake Pontiac built and sold (meaning only one to a couple may exist).<P>Like everone else said, if it's aftermarket, it's really no big deal.<P>Just my thoughts.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Shaun41178||10-05-2001||04:02 PM||||California kid said it best.  In your sig you say powersteering.  I think most thought you had the electric powersteering unit on it like what GM had developed for the 88's.<P>So someone rigged up a hydraulic powersteering unit to your car.  Big whoop-dee-doo.  You can do that to any car.  Not too impressive if you ask me.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR>Shaun41178@hotmail.com<BR>PORN FOREVER!||||reg||1
Z||000015||rockcrawl||10-05-2001||04:51 PM||||I never doubted it, I never even gave it a second thought. I never considered that it could be a factory setup, because even if one or two do exist, they are not on an '86 Fiero. It is obviously an aftermarket conversion. It is widely known that power steering conversion kits were available for the Fiero in the '80s, and there were two complete leftover kits that turned up for sale a year or two ago. Besides those kits, there were who knows how many one-off conversions done. So when someone who is a Fiero enthusiast says they have a Fiero with power steering, is there really any reason to doubt it? If someone came on here claiming to have a Fiero with factory installed power steering I could understand some skeptecism, but seriously, give the guy a break. There really are a lot of beeyatches around here. I hope I don't come accross as one of them.||||reg||7
