Z||000019||West Coast Fiero||10-05-2001||10:29 PM||||its fascinating that you claim to have a reservoir for your power steering, when infact, at a second look, it is actually a " Cool Can" fuel cooler that is designed to provide a denser charge of fuel for increased horsepower by utilizing a spiraled fuel line inside an aluminum canister which uses a sheet of cork material as a heat tranfer medium withing the canister......<P><BR>And if it was a power steering reservior why would it be mounted above the extreme temperatures of the exhaust manifold, may we see pics of the actuall steering rack. <P> In 87 GM had talked to researchers at Delphi to create an electric assist unit for the steering rack in 88 - this never happened<P>------------------<BR>Technician, West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000020||Kasdan||10-05-2001||11:48 PM||||Fuel cooler, ROFL.  Explain to me why it has a line coming from the rack and one going to the power pump, with p/s fluid in it?  funny how that works...cools fuel without coming in contact with it...thats soome d@mn good engineering if you ask me.  West Coast, i think think that you know more than you actually do.<p>[This message has been edited by Kasdan (edited 10-05-2001).]||||reg||1
