Z||000048||tomcat06085||10-06-2001||04:09 PM||||Kasdan....sorry you're taking all this flack. I didn't see this thread till a few minutes ago. Yes...I'm the tomcat that was willing to buy the unit...rack and all if needed!<P>My son is a mechanical engineer for an aerospace firm and also an ace auto mechanic. I thought the only good wrencher was myself until he got old enough to work on cars and motorcycles. Rebuilt a motorcycle transmission when he was twelve years. I had an accident that left me in a wheelchair, so when I couldn't afford the local garage my son worked on it. When the local garage couldn't find solutions, my son generally did.<P>Anyway, he has worked on Pontiacs for twenty years and told me to get an 88 Fiero if I wanted to get back to autocrossing with the use of handcontrols. I've been driving with handcontrols for thirty years, so my son made sure it was an 88 Fiero because of the suspension and the ability to make adjustments without compromising original structural design. When I mentioned Kasdan's power steering unit, he said he had been planning to use a similar design or get the plans for the electrical unit. <P>Some of us prefer power steering, some of us may need power steering. I remember when Geof Bodine had all the yahoos around New England laughing when he was engineering and introducing power steering into his stock cars. They're not laughing anymore....NASCAR is a different and better sport because of it.<P>Sorry for the grief you've received, Kasdan. I should have sent you a deposit right away.<BR><P>------------------<BR>tomcat<BR>Help me go fast!||||reg||3
